# Task scope and testing

- Before editing, state which files you expect to change.
- If the task expands into unrelated modules, stop instead of continuing opportunistically.
- Prefer a pure function plus unit test for date/time/business rules before wiring UI.
- Rust tests are mandatory for:
  - week folder calculation
  - DDL progress/thresholds
  - busy rule validation
  - calendar dedup
  - overtime 05:00 reconciliation
- For bugs, reproduce first and make the smallest fix. Do not start by refactoring.
- For UI-only tasks, do not modify Rust or DB schema.
- For DB-only tasks, do not redesign UI.
- Every TASK ends with the relevant test command or a written manual smoke-test result.
